(R/'README.md').write_text('''# Held-out source collection — collector version

Eight official notice units from WI, ME, IA, KS, OR, MN, UT and AK; eight originals and provisional distinct publication/template families; **22 input pages and74 source-reference fields**. No round2 cloud parser outputs were viewed. Native extraction was used for source navigation/transcription and is not the scored round2 native baseline.

All22 retained source-page images were inspected. Sources, unchanged-page extracts, native text, per-page images, original-to-input maps, URLs, bytes and SHA256s are retained. See source-inventory.json for the input list; each unit has fixture.json and collector-reference.json. Independent source-only adjudication is pending: these are agent collector annotations, not human gold labels or the final experiment freeze.

H06 preserves an unresolved source discrepancy: the general register box says a maximum20 calendar days; the target notice says20 working days for an extended posthearing period. The critical extension-max reference is uncertain, so provisional strict-reference eligibility is7/8. No deadline arithmetic or timezone was inferred. H07's September8 date is anticipated and explicitly NOT the effective date. H08's hearing extension retains its attendance/time condition. H02 explicitly says no public hearing.

The actual nine-original candidate retrieval ledger records the Tennessee403 and its Iowa replacement. Search order was not preregistered; collection began before the round2 protocol draft. Bucket IDs do not match the draft allocation: actual counts are two filled forms, three register notices, two clean standalone notices and one second-hearing lifecycle notice. There are no image-only scans. This is a purposive diagnostic sample; no representativeness or jurisdiction-wide discovery claim is made.

family-split.json records provisional lineage labels and explicit visual checks of the five old unnamed families (A04–A08). All eight new lineages differ by publisher/template from the old cohort and from one another; independent review must confirm this assessment. The old frozen references were not edited.

collector-freeze.json hashes this collector snapshot before independent adjudication or heldout cloud parsing. It does not freeze primary-owned arm settings, contracts or router code, nor authorize execution. Preserve this snapshot if independent review creates amended references. Source quotes may normalize whitespace and line wraps; page images remain the authority.

Collection scripts are historical provenance, not a command to re-fetch or overwrite frozen inputs. No package installation or project build was performed.
''')
